  "id": "Compound::DB00543 - Gene::3269",
  "verbalization": "Amoxapine is implicated in the relationship with Hrh1 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Amoxapine binds to Hrh4, which is involved in histamine receptor activity, and this activity is further participated by Hrh1. Similarly, Amoxapine is linked to Hrh4 through a pathway that involves histamine receptors, which are also participated by Hrh1. These connections imply a potential role for Amoxapine in modulating histamine receptor function, with Hrh1 being a downstream participant in this process. \n\nThe evidence is further supported by the fact that Amoxapine causes Painful Ejaculation, which is caused by Desipramine, and Desipramine binds to Hrh1. This suggests that Amoxapine may influence Hrh1 through a broader pharmacological mechanism, possibly involving the Tricyclic Antidepressant class of compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Amoxapine could interact with Hrh1, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
